{"term":"vow","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:82e59846bf84657896","definition":"A solemn promise to perform some act, or behave in a specified manner, especially a promise to live and act in accordance with the rules of a religious order.","example":"The old hermit, up in the mountains, took a vow of silence.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["break-vow","exchange vows","marriage vow","renew one's vows","solemn vow","take vows","vowess","vowless","vowmaker","vowmaking","vow of celibacy","wedding vow"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vow#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:970f16a742c1a385b3","definition":"A declaration or assertion.","example":"Swearing doesn't just mean what we now understand by \"dirty words\". It is entwined, in social and linguistic history, with the other sort of swearing: vows and oaths. Consider for a moment the origins of almost any word we have for bad language – \"profanity\", \"curses\", \"oaths\" and \"swearing\" itself.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["break-vow","exchange vows","marriage vow","renew one's vows","solemn vow","take vows","vowess","vowless","vowmaker","vowmaking","vow of celibacy","wedding vow"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vow#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:236c7291263da612db","definition":"A votive offering.","example":"There are also waxen vows, that represent other parts of the body mixed with them; but of these there are few in comparison of the number of the Priapi.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete","wordFamily":["break-vow","exchange vows","marriage vow","renew one's vows","solemn vow","t